  "goodToKnow": "Die Volkspartei is a people's party, a big-tent party that aims to appeal to voters across social classes rather than one group. In post-war Germany, CDU/CSU and SPD were the classic Volksparteien, each regularly winning 40 percent or more. Since the 2010s their combined share has fallen sharply, and commentators talk about das Ende der Volksparteien. Das Volk means the people. Plural: die Volksparteien."
